an Sauma begins an embassy to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#europe">Europe</a> seeking an alliance against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#mamluk">Mamluks</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1295</span><span class="rf-text">Ghazan converts to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#islam">Islam</a> and begins sweeping reforms with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rashid-al-din-hamadani">Rashid al-Din</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1299</span><span class="rf-text">Ghazan wins at Wadi al-Khaznadar, briefly taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#damascus">Damascus</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1318</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rashid-al-din-hamadani">Rashid al-Din</a>, the state's ablest administrator, is executed</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1335</span><span class="rf-text">Abu Said dies without an heir and the Ilkhanate fragments</span></li></ol>
